  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-005",
   "finding": "report #15",
   "old": "Hesai's SPAD IP (intellectual property, here mainly patents) comes from this spin-off of EPFL (the Swiss federal technology institute in Lausanne) and TU Delft (Delft University of Technology), bought in late 2023.",
   "new": "Part of Hesai's SPAD IP (intellectual property, here mainly patents) comes from this spin-off of EPFL (the Swiss federal technology institute in Lausanne) and TU Delft (Delft University of Technology), bought in late 2023; Hesai says it had also researched SPADs itself since 2016.",
   "why": "Stops overstating: only part of Hesai's SPAD IP came from Fastree3D."
  },
  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-006",
   "finding": "report §3 flag 12; report #7 (partial) and #40",
   "old": "Scantinel's assets went for \\$0.4 M after a €10 M round, and Ibeo went for ≈€20 M out of insolvency (§C3a).\n- **Per share, a soft landing rather than a win.** About CHF 6.7 M over 429,444 shares is ≈CHF 15–16 per share, below every 2016–20 conversion price (CHF 27–48). Hesai's filings show no contingent consideration, later acquisition payments or goodwill, so no material earn-out (a later payment that depends on performance) was made [P/E]. Unless liquidation preferences (terms that repay some investors first in a sale) changed the split (not public), money invested from 2016 lost value while founders' shares at par (bought at nominal value) and the earliest money gained [U on terms].",
   "new": "Scantinel's assets went for \\$0.4 M, plus a \\$1.8 M operating advance, after a €10 M round, and Ibeo went for ≈€20 M out of insolvency (§C3a).\n- **Per share, a soft landing rather than a win.** The \\$7.67 M price is about CHF 6.7 M. Taking the CHF 429,444 of capital as 429,444 shares of CHF 1 nominal [U], that is $6.7\\times10^{6}/429{,}444\\approx15.6$ CHF per share, below every 2016–20 conversion price (CHF 27–48). Hesai's filings show no contingent consideration, later acquisition payments or goodwill, so no material earn-out (a later payment that depends on performance) was made [P/E]. Liquidation preferences (terms that repay some investors first in a sale) could change how the proceeds were split, but their terms are not public [U]. Without them, money invested from 2016 lost value, while the founders' shares, bought at par (nominal value), and the earliest money gained.",
   "why": "Aligns the Scantinel price with §C3a (\\$0.4 M plus a \\$1.8 M operating advance). Shows the per-share division, flags the CHF 1 nominal assumption [U], and splits the 40-word sentence."
  },
  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-007",
   "finding": "report #40; report §3 flag 15",
   "old": "World-class European SPAD and TDC know-how (the lineage from Canesta to Kinect, EPFL AQUA, TU Delft) could not reach automotive scale on about \\$6 M, but it did not die: a Chinese maker with volume bought it as a going concern (a functioning company, not a liquidation) at roughly the capital invested. The disclosed IP lineage supports treating Hesai's FTX and Picasso as **distinct designs**, though public information does not expose die or wafer provenance.\n- It mirrors the wider pattern in Parts B and D,",
   "new": "World-class European SPAD and TDC know-how, from Canesta and Kinect to EPFL's AQUA lab and TU Delft, could not reach automotive scale on about \\$6 M. It did not die, however: a Chinese maker with volume bought it as a going concern, a functioning company rather than a liquidation, at roughly the capital invested. The disclosed IP lineage supports treating Hesai's FTX and Picasso as **distinct designs**, though public information does not expose die or wafer provenance.\n- It mirrors the wider pattern described in §B3, §C3a and §G2,",
   "why": "Splits the 54-word Reading sentence and removes the nested parentheticals. Points to where the MicroVision consolidation is actually described (§B3, §C3a, §G2), not Part D."
  },
  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-008",
   "finding": "report §3 flag 14",
   "old": "joint development with Adaps ran from 2020 until early 2023",
   "new": "joint development with Adaps ran from 2019 or 2020 (sources differ) until early 2023",
   "why": "Matches the table row: sources differ on whether the Adaps work began in 2019 or 2020."
  },
  {
