   "finding": "report #33",
   "old": "true photon arrival rate $n$ (s⁻¹) and dead time $\\tau_d$ (s), the recorded count rate $m$ (s⁻¹) is\n\n    $$m=n\\,e^{-n\\tau_d} \\tag{76}$$\n\n  - [E] Eq. (76) peaks at $n=1/\\tau_d$",
   "new": "true photon arrival rate $r$ (s⁻¹, per SPAD, the symbol used in §C6(d)) and dead time $\\tau_d$ (s), the recorded count rate $m$ (s⁻¹) is\n\n    $$m=r\\,e^{-r\\tau_d} \\tag{76}$$\n\n  - [E] Eq. (76) peaks at $r=1/\\tau_d$",
   "why": "Writes Eq. (76) with r, the per-SPAD rate used in §C6(d) Eq. (82), instead of n."
  },
  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-013",
   "finding": "report §3 flag 9",
   "old": "Bright sunlight adds ≈10⁴ background counts per point (§C6(d)), which dwarfs them.",
   "new": "Bright sunlight adds thousands of background counts per point (≈5,960 in the central case of §C0 subsection 10.3, built from the rates of §C6(d)), which dwarfs them.",
