   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-028",
   "finding": "report §3 flag 20",
   "old": "2. **A peer-reviewed PDE roadmap that products follow within 2–4 years.** Examples: 36.5% in 2023 research became 37% in the 2025 product; 42.5% at 940 nm was reached in 2025 research.",
   "new": "2. **A peer-reviewed PDE roadmap that products have so far followed within about two years.** The one clear example: 36.5% at 940 nm in 2023 research, on a 6 µm pixel, became 37% in the 2025 product, on a 10 µm pixel. Research reached 42.5% at 940 nm in 2025.",
   "why": "'2-4 years' rested on one two-year example that also changes pixel size."
  },
  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-029",
   "finding": "report #21",
   "old": "\"Line mode only\" and a ≈6 ns dead time tie IMX479 to one-axis scanned architectures.",
   "new": "\"Line mode only\" ties IMX479 to one-axis scanned architectures. Its ≈6 ns dead time also leaves each SPAD blind for about a third of the time in bright sun at 940 nm behind a 10 nm filter (29–33%, §C6(d)).",
   "why": "Line mode, not dead time, ties IMX479 to scanning; says what the dead time does, hedged for paralyzability."
  },
  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-030",
   "finding": "report #37",
   "old": "Sony's 37% for IMX479 is a **product PDE** at ≈3 V excess bias.",
   "new": "Sony's 37% for IMX479 is a **product PDE**, at ≈3 V excess bias if the 3.3 V $V_{\\rm EX}$ supply is the excess bias (§C5a) [E].",
   "why": "The ~3 V excess bias is inferred from the 3.3 V V_EX supply, not disclosed."
  },
  {
   "id": "06_C5_C5a_C6-031",
   "finding": "symbol scheme",
   "old": "$R=c\\Delta t/2$, where $R$ is the range, $c$ the speed of light and $\\Delta t$ the round-trip delay: a target 100 m away returns after about $\\Delta t=2R/c",
