   "old": "with about 0.45–0.55× the solar irradiance of 905 nm. The ratio varies with humidity and passband: the ASTM G173 values of §C4c give $0.303/0.693=0.44$ for ±10 nm band averages and $0.472/0.817=0.58$ at the exact wavelengths. At 1550 nm the reference value is about 0.35× ($0.27/0.82=0.33$ to $0.27/0.69=0.39$), with a larger permitted average power under the particular Class 1 comparison in §C4.",
   "new": "with about 0.44–0.58× the solar irradiance of 905 nm. The ratio varies with humidity and passband: the ASTM G173 values of §C4c give $0.303/0.693=0.44$ for ±10 nm band averages and $0.472/0.817=0.58$ at the exact wavelengths. At 1,550 nm the reference value is 0.33–0.39× ($0.270/0.817=0.33$ against the exact 905 nm value, $0.270/0.693=0.39$ against the band average), with a larger permitted average power under the particular Class 1 comparison of §C4c, subsection 1.",
